PREDECESSOR REUSE (DRY — a complete P4 ConflictWarnings parity core already exists)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, proven P4 feature-view surface already ships the ConflictWarnings parity core at
`apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/ConflictWarnings.*` (0084). It owns, as PUBLIC, dependency-free
types in the same TeslaSync module:
  - `AutomationConflict` + `ConflictWarningsAutomationConflictSeverity` (web @/api/types shape; severity→icon)
  - `ConflictWarningRow` (display row: web `${automation_id}-${index}` key + `"{name}": {reason}` detail)
  - `ConflictWarningsProjection.rows(from:)` (order-stable projection)
  - `ConflictWarningsRender` (.loading/.failed/.empty/.conflicts(rows)) + the state VIEWS
    `ConflictWarningsList` / `ConflictWarningsEmpty` / `ConflictWarningsError` / `ConflictWarningsLoading`
  - `CWCopy.title` == "automations.builder.conflict" → "Potential Conflict"
My first draft DUPLICATED these (defining its own `AutomationConflict`/severity/row/banner) and COLLIDED
("'AutomationConflict' is ambiguous for type lookup" ×8 in the real app-target compile — see build #1).
Per DRY + the engineering guidelines (reuse a shared util rather than duplicate), the P7 page was
rewritten to REUSE the existing parity core verbatim and add ONLY the navigable-page layer with
unique, collision-free `…Page…`-prefixed names. The web-source string + all 4 data states are honored
through that reuse — no parity narrowing (covenant #2/#5/#7).

NAVIGATION (the unit is (unrouted)):
The web `ConflictWarnings` is a SECTION the `/automations` automation builder renders inline (beside the
rule editor) — NOT a standalone route. So this unit does NOT take a top-level `AppRoute` (that would
hijack the builder's route). Instead it ships a typed `NavigationDestination` seam —
`ConflictWarningsPageLink` + `View.conflictWarningsPageDestination()` +
`ConflictWarningsPageRouteRegistration.make(...)` — that any `NavigationStack` adopts to deep-link the
full-screen conflict list. No edits to the P4 shell (AppShell/AppRoute/TeslaSyncApp) or to the existing
0084 feature-view were made (covenant #7).

